From bb5cc6809132900fd54a6a9cd03c8af155a21839 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Baily Zhang <blitheshuo@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 09:43:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(cli): drain lifecycle hooks before exit and align
 observer hook cwd

Review follow-ups for the observer lifecycle hook events:

- Drain in-flight hook runs before ExitHandler.exit() in the headless
  RunController (success and rethrow paths): DI teardown disposes the
  HookExecutor before the lifecycle service and kills any still-active
  hook process, which silently terminated Stop hooks spawned at stream
  settle. HookLifecycleService now exposes drain(), capped at 5s to
  mirror the shutdown timeout, and disposeAsync() reuses it.
- Resolve observer hook cwd from the configured workspace root
  (workspaceFolders[0], the same directory SessionStart hooks receive)
  instead of the raw launch cwd, so project hook configs are found
  consistently when running from a subdirectory.
- Always warn on non-zero observer hook exits, even without stderr, so
  killed or signal-terminated hooks are not silent.
- Reword the types header to CC-style (PermissionRequest is not a
  Claude Code event name).
- Tests: exit-ordering tests for RunController draining, drain() unit
  tests, workspace-root cwd test, TestLogger assertions for hook
  failure and empty-stderr warnings.

Related to #2684

Signed-off-by: Baily Zhang <blitheshuo@gmail.com>
