From 21940d9a4ac54eae701e5e25acee62de861ccc47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Baily Zhang <blitheshuo@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 13:49:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(cli): capture session id for SessionEnd and memoize
 observer hook cwd

AI review follow-ups for the observer lifecycle hook events:

- Remember the session id of the most recent dispatch so SessionEnd can
  still be attributed to the session that ran when the active session is
  already cleared during container disposal (falls back to the active
  session when nothing was captured).
- Memoize the resolved workspace root so every event of the session
  reports the same cwd even if the configured workspace changes
  mid-session, matching what the SessionStart alignment promises.
- Log a warning when drain() hits its 5s cap, including how many hook
  runs were still in flight, instead of timing out silently.
- Document that dispatched events are fire-and-forget notifications
  with no cross-turn ordering guarantees, so consumers must not treat
  the sequence as a strict state machine.

Related to #2684

Signed-off-by: Baily Zhang <blitheshuo@gmail.com>
